{
  "_comment": [
    "Synthetic gen4 Platinum scenario (plan 2.7 for gen4; decision 6 says a recording needs Scott):",
    "a new game, the starter, a route change, one wild battle, one Leader Roark battle, a level up,",
    "a blackout and a reset. It is built to touch the hooks in gen4's mounted():",
    "The Oreburgh part starts at 62 s so the Roark split lands after the timer's first minute:",
    "  known-legacy-bugs.md #33 (a numeric sub-minute split time) would otherwise throw in both apps.",
    "  flags.new_game_1 false -> true          new run (startTime, attempt++, ROM starter writes)",
    "  overworld.map_name change              OBS 'Map Change - <map>' marker",
    "  battle.mode 'Wild'                     queued 'IN - Wild' marker",
    "  battle.opponent.trainer set / null     'IN - Leader Roark' / 'OUT - Leader Roark' markers",
    "  meta.state 'From Battle' with a split trainer",
    "                                         Full/Deprecated/Simple split CSVs, right_ui -> Splits",
    "  player.team.0.level change             level-up handling",
    "  battle.player.team.0.stats.hp -> 0 in Battle",
    "                                         blackout",
    "  flags.new_game_1 true -> false         reset (playerResets++, OBS 'RESET')",
    "Referenced properties carry the glossary value the recorder would have written (a species",
    "or trainer name), as the gen1 scenario does. Every path is checked against the mapper XML",
    "at build time. Values are plausible, not a real run: this fixture proves determinism and",
    "no-change-under-refactor, never correctness (see make-fixture.ts)."
  ],
